Cell["Campaign → Voting → In Office", "Subsubsection"],

Cell["Campaign creates candidates by mutating the proposed TNN parameters. Voting scores those candidates using a fixed set of criteria. In Office uses the winning output and retains the TNN that produced it, together with the context that establishes its field of expertise.", "Text"],

Cell["The initial voting idea favors clear, predominant outputs with lower entropy. In the toy experiment, task feedback must also show whether the chosen behavior works: a confident output can still select the wrong move. Deterministic scoring makes the decision repeatable for a fixed candidate set; it does not make candidate generation deterministic.", "Text"],

Cell["The arrows show the intended staged data flow. The supplied TGP snippet names the generators and selection steps; context passing, compatibility checks and candidate scoring remain implementation details.", "Text"]

}, Open]]

}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["", "SlideShowNavigationBar", CellTags->"SlideShowHeader", CellOpen->False],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["TNN lifecycle", "Section"],

Cell["For each context, the system first looks for a TNN with a matching field of expertise. A match reuses the existing specialist. Otherwise, the TGP creates a new one.", "Text"],

