  InsetBox[StyleBox["MNN suite", FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro", FontSize->13.5, FontWeight->"Bold", FontColor->RGBColor[0.89, 0.915, 0.945], TextAlignment->Center], {830, 241}, Center],
  InsetBox[StyleBox["promote the accepted update", FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro", FontSize->11.5, FontWeight->"Plain", FontColor->RGBColor[0.61, 0.67, 0.75], TextAlignment->Center], {830, 217}, Center],
  {FaceForm[RGBColor[0.086, 0.105, 0.133]], EdgeForm[Directive[RGBColor[0.235, 0.279, 0.337], AbsoluteThickness[1.25]]], RectangleBox[{375, 32}, {625, 98}, RoundingRadius->9]},
  InsetBox[StyleBox["Keep current suite", FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro", FontSize->13.5, FontWeight->"Bold", FontColor->RGBColor[0.89, 0.915, 0.945], TextAlignment->Center], {500, 76}, Center],
  InsetBox[StyleBox["if validation fails", FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro", FontSize->11.5, FontWeight->"Plain", FontColor->RGBColor[0.61, 0.67, 0.75], TextAlignment->Center], {500, 52}, Center],
  InsetBox[StyleBox["Pass", FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro", FontSize->11.5, FontWeight->"Plain", FontColor->RGBColor[0.35, 0.79, 0.72], TextAlignment->Center], {665, 252}, Center],
  InsetBox[StyleBox["Regression", FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro", FontSize->11.5, FontWeight->"Plain", FontColor->RGBColor[0.35, 0.79, 0.72], TextAlignment->Center], {550, 146}, Center]
}, ImageSize->940, AspectRatio->0.47, PlotRange->{{0, 1000}, {0, 470}}, PlotRangePadding->None, ImagePadding->0, Background->RGBColor[0.055, 0.067, 0.086]]
], "Diagram", Evaluatable->False, CellTags->"diagram:mtp"],

Cell["If the update fails those checks, the current suite stays in use. This feedback loop is the proposed route to better initial TNNs over time; the notebook does not claim measured improvement. The short MTP function below marks the training entry point, while validation and promotion remain to be implemented.", "Text"]

}, Open]]

}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["", "SlideShowNavigationBar", CellTags->"SlideShowHeader", CellOpen->False],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["A toy problem: red and blue tiles", "Section"],

Cell["The proposed test uses a grid with two tile types. Blue and red tiles have different mappings from the agent’s four move commands to physical directions. The goal is to see whether the system can keep a useful specialist through small changes, then generate another one when the changed surroundings require different behavior.", "Text"],

Cell["The supplied environment already defines the board, the player position, a local view and basic movement. With the default settings, the board is 16 × 16, the agent starts at row 8 and column 0, and radius 1 gives a local window of up to 3 × 3 cells. Blue becomes less likely down the board as red becomes more likely. A run finishes when the agent reaches the last row.", "Text"],

Cell["The tile-dependent direction mappings are part of the proposed experiment. Env.move() currently applies the four directions directly, so those mappings and the learning behavior are not yet implemented in this skeleton. The code is kept exactly as supplied.", "Text"],

Cell["A useful trial begins with familiar local contexts, introduces a few changed tiles, then exposes the agent to enough of the other tile system to make the old specialist a poor match. The expected pattern to test is reuse, generation, and then reuse of the new specialist. A small visual change alone should not force a new TNN if the current behavior still works.", "Text"],

Cell["To assess that pattern, a later implementation can record when generation happens, which TNN is selected, how long specialists remain active, and whether the agent reaches the goal. These are proposed observations for the experiment, rather than results from the current template.", "Text"]

}, Open]]

}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["", "SlideShowNavigationBar", CellTags->"SlideShowHeader", CellOpen->False],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Python structure", "Section"],

Cell["The seven modules below appear in the supplied order. Each code block preserves the original text, including indentation, alignment, naming and ellipses. They document the architecture and are not evaluated by this notebook.", "Text"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["defval.py · Default network definitions", "Subsection"],

Cell["This module reserves the layer sizes, activation functions, weights and biases for the TNN and each MNN. The empty lists leave the baseline configuration open while keeping the same four-part description across every network type.", "Text"],

Cell["#defval.py\n\nfrom netdef import Cube, Grid\n\nTNN_LAYERSIZE: list[int]   = []\nTNN_ACTIVFUNC: list        = []\nTNN_WEIGVALUE: Cube[float] = []\nTNN_BIASVALUE: Grid[float] = []\n\nSNN_LAYERSIZE: list[int]   = []\nSNN_ACTIVFUNC: list        = []\nSNN_WEIGVALUE: Cube[float] = []\nSNN_BIASVALUE: Grid[float] = []\n\nANN_LAYERSIZE: list[int]   = []\nANN_ACTIVFUNC: list        = []\nANN_WEIGVALUE: Cube[float] = []\nANN_BIASVALUE: Grid[float] = []\n\nWNN_LAYERSIZE: list[int]   = []\nWNN_ACTIVFUNC: list        = []\nWNN_WEIGVALUE: Cube[float] = []\nWNN_BIASVALUE: Grid[float] = []\n\nBNN_LAYERSIZE: list[int]   = []\nBNN_ACTIVFUNC: list        = []\nBNN_WEIGVALUE: Cube[float] = []\nBNN_BIASVALUE: Grid[float] = []", "Program",
 Evaluatable->False,
 AutoIndent->False,
 LineBreakWithin->False,
 PageWidth->Infinity,
 CellTags->"code:defval.py"]

}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["envdef.py · The environment and local context", "Subsection"],

Cell["Specs holds the grid settings and display values. numgrid() builds the red-and-blue distribution, while strgrid() renders it. Env owns the current position, clamps movement at the board edges, and exposes both a full view and the nearby context through near().", "Text"],

Cell["The random generator is created once with Random(42). The near() window is clipped at the board boundaries, so the template leaves the later network implementation to decide how observations of different sizes will be represented.", "Text"],

Cell["# envdef.py\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom enum import auto, Enum\nfrom random import Random\n\nfrom netdef import Grid\n\nansiblu = \"\\033[34m\"\nansired = \"\\033[31m\"\nansirst = \"\\033[0m\"\nansicls = \"\\033[2J\\033[H\"\n\nrandgen = Random(42)\n\n\nclass Move(Enum):\n    Up = auto()\n    Dn = auto()\n    Lf = auto()\n    Rg = auto()\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Specs:\n    bluini: int = 16\n    bludif: int = 1\n    bluval: int = 0\n    blustr: str = ansiblu + \"B\" + ansirst\n\n    redini: int = 0\n    reddif: int = 1\n    redval: int = 1\n    redstr: str = ansired + \"R\" + ansirst\n\n    youval: int = 2\n    youstr: str = \"Y\"\n\n    rownum: int = 16\n    rowini: int = 8\n\n    colnum: int = 16\n    colini: int = 0\n\n    sedval: int = 42\n    radius: int = 1\n\n\ndef numgrid(specs: Specs) -> Grid[int]:\n    probblu = specs.bluini\n    probred = specs.redini\n    newgrid = []\n    tilpick = 0\n\n    for _ in range(specs.rownum):\n        probblu -= specs.bludif if probblu > 0 else 0\n        probred += specs.reddif if probred >= 0 else 0\n\n        temprow = []\n        for _ in range(specs.colnum):\n            tilpick = randgen.choices([specs.bluval, specs.redval], [probblu, probred])[0]\n            temprow.append(tilpick)\n        newgrid.append(temprow)\n\n    return newgrid\n\n\ndef strgrid(grid: Grid[int], specs: Specs) -> str:\n    newgrid = []\n\n    blu_youval = specs.youval + specs.bluval\n    red_youval = specs.youval + specs.redval\n\n    for row in grid:\n        temprow = \"\"\n        for cel in row:\n            if cel == specs.bluval:\n                temprow += specs.blustr\n            if cel == specs.redval:\n                temprow += specs.redstr\n            if cel == blu_youval:\n                temprow += specs.youstr\n            if cel == red_youval:\n                temprow += specs.youstr\n        newgrid.append(temprow)\n\n    return \"\\n\".join(newgrid)\n\n\nclass Env:\n    def __init__(self, specs: Specs = Specs()) -> None:\n        self.mygrid = numgrid(specs)\n        self.myspec = specs\n        self.rowcur = specs.rowini\n        self.colcur = specs.colini\n\n    def __str__(self) -> str:\n        return strgrid(self.view(), self.myspec)\n\n    def done(self) -> bool:\n        return bool(self.rowcur == self.myspec.rownum - 1)\n\n    def move(self, move: Move) -> None:\n        if move == Move.Up:\n            self.rowcur -= 1\n        if move == Move.Dn:\n            self.rowcur += 1\n        if move == Move.Lf:\n            self.colcur -= 1\n        if move == Move.Rg:\n            self.colcur += 1\n\n        self.rowcur = max(0, min(self.rowcur, self.myspec.rownum - 1))\n        self.colcur = max(0, min(self.colcur, self.myspec.colnum - 1))\n\n    def view(self) -> Grid[int]:\n        grid = [row[:] for row in self.mygrid]\n        grid[self.rowcur][self.colcur] += self.myspec.youval\n        return grid\n\n    def near(self) -> Grid[int]:\n        grid = self.view()\n\n        rowmax = min(self.myspec.rownum, self.rowcur + self.myspec.radius + 1)\n        rowmin = max(0, self.rowcur - self.myspec.radius)\n\n        colmax = min(self.myspec.colnum, self.colcur + self.myspec.radius + 1)\n        colmin = max(0, self.colcur - self.myspec.radius)\n\n        return [row[colmin:colmax] for row in grid[rowmin:rowmax]]", "Program",
 Evaluatable->False,
 AutoIndent->False,
 LineBreakWithin->False,
 PageWidth->Infinity,
 CellTags->"code:envdef.py"]

}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["jitdef.py · Shared state and the runtime loop", "Subsection"],

Cell["Ctx collects the environment, timing fields, TNN queues and the four MNNs. The jitml() loop makes the intended order visible: check completion, render, handle lifecycle work, request generation when needed, make a move, and check whether meta-training is due.", "Text"],

Cell["The queues and Step methods mark the boundaries between those responsibilities. Their detailed policies remain open, so the notebook can explain the system without choosing a full implementation.", "Text"],

Cell["# jitdef.py\n\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\n\nfrom envdef import Env\nfrom netdef import Ann, Bnn, Snn, Wnn, Que, Tnn\nfrom stepdef import Step\n\n\n@dataclass\nclass Ctx:\n    runme: bool = True\n\n    every: int = 32\n    ticks: int = 64\n    clock: int = 0\n\n    myenv: Env = Env()\n\n    myque: Que = []\n    okque: Que = []\n    dfque: Que = [Tnn()]\n\n    mysnn: Snn = Snn()\n    myann: Ann = Ann()\n    mywnn: Wnn = Wnn()\n    mybnn: Bnn = Bnn()\n\n\ndef jitml(ctx: Ctx) -> None:\n    while ctx.runme:\n        Step.doneplay(ctx)\n        Step.uirender(ctx)\n        Step.keepbusy(ctx)\n        Step.killdead(ctx)\n        Step.givelife(ctx)\n        Step.needstgp(ctx)\n        Step.makemove(ctx)\n        Step.needsmtp(ctx)", "Program",
 Evaluatable->False,
 AutoIndent->False,
 LineBreakWithin->False,
 PageWidth->Infinity,
 CellTags->"code:jitdef.py"]

}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["mtpdef.py · The meta-training entry point", "Subsection"],

Cell["MTP() sends the current TNN queue to each generator’s trainme() method. It is the compact entry point for the learning phase described above. Extracting training pairs, fitting each MNN and deciding whether to accept an update belong inside the later training and validation implementation.", "Text"],

Cell["# mtpdef.py\n\nfrom jitdef import Ctx\n\n\ndef MTP(ctx: Ctx) -> None:\n    ctx.mysnn.trainme(ctx.myque)\n    ctx.myann.trainme(ctx.myque)\n    ctx.mywnn.trainme(ctx.myque)\n    ctx.mybnn.trainme(ctx.myque)", "Program",
 Evaluatable->False,
 AutoIndent->False,
 LineBreakWithin->False,
 PageWidth->Infinity,
 CellTags->"code:mtpdef.py"]

}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["netdef.py · Network types and generation interfaces", "Subsection"],

Cell["Grid, Cube and Tess describe nested list shapes, while Ten names the tensor type. Net stores a common network definition, its current and past inputs, and the fields used for matching and lifecycle decisions.", "Text"],

Cell["Tnn adds the move-generation interface. Snn, Ann, Wnn and Bnn each expose the part of a new TNN they are responsible for producing. The forward(), trainme() and generation methods intentionally remain placeholders. Their bodies, type syntax, spacing and class layout are preserved below.", "Text"],

Cell["# netdef.py\n\nfrom torch import Tensor\n\nimport defval\nfrom envdef import Move\n\ntype Mnn = Snn | Ann | Wnn | Bnn\ntype Que = list[Tnn]\n\ntype Grid[T] = list[list[T]]\ntype Cube[T] = list[Grid[T]]\ntype Tess[T] = list[Cube[T]]\n\ntype Ten = Tensor\n\n\nclass Net:\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        layersize: list[int],\n        activfunc: list,\n        weigvalue: Cube[float],\n        biasvalue: Grid[float],\n        currinput: Grid[int],\n        pastinput: Cube[int],\n        lifescore: int,\n        lifelimit: int,\n        goodmatch: bool\n    ) -> None:\n        self.layersize = layersize\n        self.activfunc = activfunc\n        self.weigvalue = weigvalue\n        self.biasvalue = biasvalue\n        self.currinput = currinput\n        self.pastinput = pastinput\n        self.lifescore = lifescore\n        self.lifelimit = lifelimit\n        self.goodmatch = goodmatch\n\n    def forward(self, ten: Ten) -> ...:\n        ...\n\n    def trainme(self, que: Que) -> ...:\n        ...\n\n\nclass Tnn(Net):\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        layersize: None | list[int]   = None,\n        activfunc: None | list        = None,\n        weigvalue: None | Cube[float] = None,\n        biasvalue: None | Grid[float] = None,\n        currinput: None | Grid[int]   = None,\n        pastinput: None | Cube[int]   = None,\n        lifescore: None | int         = None,\n        lifelimit: None | int         = None,\n        goodmatch: None | bool        = None\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(\n            layersize or defval.TNN_LAYERSIZE,\n            activfunc or defval.TNN_ACTIVFUNC,\n            weigvalue or defval.TNN_WEIGVALUE,\n            biasvalue or defval.TNN_BIASVALUE,\n            currinput or [],\n            pastinput or [],\n            lifescore or 10,\n            lifelimit or 0,\n            goodmatch or False)\n\n    def gen_takenmove(self) -> Move:\n        ...\n\n\nclass Snn(Net):\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        layersize: None | list[int]   = None,\n        activfunc: None | list        = None,\n        weigvalue: None | Cube[float] = None,\n        biasvalue: None | Grid[float] = None,\n        currinput: None | Grid[int]   = None,\n        pastinput: None | Cube[int]   = None,\n        lifescore: None | int         = None,\n        lifelimit: None | int         = None,\n        goodmatch: None | bool        = None\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(\n            layersize or defval.SNN_LAYERSIZE,\n            activfunc or defval.SNN_ACTIVFUNC,\n            weigvalue or defval.SNN_WEIGVALUE,\n            biasvalue or defval.SNN_BIASVALUE,\n            currinput or [],\n            pastinput or [],\n            lifescore or 10,\n            lifelimit or 0,\n            goodmatch or False)\n\n    def gen_layersize(self) -> list[int]:\n        ...\n\n\nclass Ann(Net):\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        layersize: None | list[int]   = None,\n        activfunc: None | list        = None,\n        weigvalue: None | Cube[float] = None,\n        biasvalue: None | Grid[float] = None,\n        currinput: None | Grid[int]   = None,\n        pastinput: None | Cube[int]   = None,\n        lifescore: None | int         = None,\n        lifelimit: None | int         = None,\n        goodmatch: None | bool        = None\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(\n            layersize or defval.ANN_LAYERSIZE,\n            activfunc or defval.ANN_ACTIVFUNC,\n            weigvalue or defval.ANN_WEIGVALUE,\n            biasvalue or defval.ANN_BIASVALUE,\n            currinput or [],\n            pastinput or [],\n            lifescore or 10,\n            lifelimit or 0,\n            goodmatch or False)\n\n    def gen_activfunc(self) -> list:\n        ...\n\nclass Wnn(Net):\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        layersize: None | list[int]   = None,\n        activfunc: None | list        = None,\n        weigvalue: None | Cube[float] = None,\n        biasvalue: None | Grid[float] = None,\n        currinput: None | Grid[int]   = None,\n        pastinput: None | Cube[int]   = None,\n        lifescore: None | int         = None,\n        lifelimit: None | int         = None,\n        goodmatch: None | bool        = None\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(\n            layersize or defval.WNN_LAYERSIZE,\n            activfunc or defval.WNN_ACTIVFUNC,\n            weigvalue or defval.WNN_WEIGVALUE,\n            biasvalue or defval.WNN_BIASVALUE,\n            currinput or [],\n            pastinput or [],\n            lifescore or 10,\n            lifelimit or 0,\n            goodmatch or False)\n\n    def gen_weigvalue(self) -> Cube[float]:\n        ...\n\nclass Bnn(Net):\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        layersize: None | list[int]   = None,\n        activfunc: None | list        = None,\n        weigvalue: None | Cube[float] = None,\n        biasvalue: None | Grid[float] = None,\n        currinput: None | Grid[int]   = None,\n        pastinput: None | Cube[int]   = None,\n        lifescore: None | int         = None,\n        lifelimit: None | int         = None,\n        goodmatch: None | bool        = None\n    ) -> None:\n        super().__init__(\n            layersize or defval.BNN_LAYERSIZE,\n            activfunc or defval.BNN_ACTIVFUNC,\n            weigvalue or defval.BNN_WEIGVALUE,\n            biasvalue or defval.BNN_BIASVALUE,\n            currinput or [],\n            pastinput or [],\n            lifescore or 10,\n            lifelimit or 0,\n            goodmatch or False)\n\n    def gen_biasvalue(self) -> Grid[float]:\n        ...", "Program",
 Evaluatable->False,
 AutoIndent->False,
 LineBreakWithin->False,
 PageWidth->Infinity,
 CellTags->"code:netdef.py"]

}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["stepdef.py · The runtime decisions", "Subsection"],

Cell["is_match() and is_alive() name the two central decisions: whether a TNN fits the context and whether it should remain available. Step separates rendering, lifecycle work, movement, task generation and meta-training into individual hooks called by the main loop.", "Text"],

Cell["This keeps the overall runtime sequence easy to inspect while leaving matching rules, lifetime updates and scheduling for the implementation stage.", "Text"],

Cell["# stepdef.py\n\nfrom jitdef import Ctx\nfrom netdef import Tnn\nfrom mtpdef import MTP\nfrom tgpdef import TGP\n\n\ndef is_match(tnn: Tnn, ctx: Ctx) -> bool:\n    ...\n\n\ndef is_alive(tnn: Tnn) -> bool:\n    ...\n\n\nclass Step:\n    @staticmethod\n    def doneplay(ctx: Ctx) -> None:\n        ...\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def uirender(ctx: Ctx) -> None:\n        ...\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def keepbusy(ctx: Ctx) -> None:\n        ...\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def killdead(ctx: Ctx) -> None:\n        ...\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def givelife(ctx: Ctx) -> None:\n        ...\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def makemove(ctx: Ctx) -> None:\n        ...\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def needstgp(ctx: Ctx) -> None:\n        ...\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def needsmtp(ctx: Ctx) -> None:\n        ...", "Program",
 Evaluatable->False,
 AutoIndent->False,
 LineBreakWithin->False,
 PageWidth->Infinity,
 CellTags->"code:stepdef.py"]

}, Open]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["tgpdef.py · From proposals to a task network", "Subsection"],

Cell["TGP() reads the nearby grid, asks the four MNNs for initial definitions, creates candidate sets, selects values through Vote, and returns a Tnn. The names mirror the proposed generation and election process.", "Text"],

Cell["The current skeleton collects the context but does not yet pass it through the generators. It also votes on the definition fields separately. A later implementation must connect the staged inputs and keep the selected shape, activations, weights and biases compatible; the supplied snippet remains unchanged.", "Text"],

Cell["# tgpdef.py\n\nfrom jitdef import Ctx\nfrom netdef import Cube, Grid, Tess, Tnn\n\n\nclass Vote:\n    @staticmethod\n    def layersize_from(cands: Grid[int]) -> list[int]:\n        ...\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def activfunc_from(cands: Grid) -> list:\n        ...\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def weigvalue_from(cands: Tess[float]) -> Cube[float]:\n        ...\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def biasvalue_from(cands: Cube[float]) -> Grid[float]:\n        ...\n\n\ndef candidates_of[T](L: list[T]) -> Grid[T]:\n    ...\n\n\ndef TGP(ctx: Ctx) -> Tnn:\n    grid = ctx.myenv.near()\n\n    laysinit = ctx.mysnn.gen_layersize()\n    actiinit = ctx.myann.gen_activfunc()\n    weiginit = ctx.mywnn.gen_weigvalue()\n    biasinit = ctx.mybnn.gen_biasvalue()\n\n    layscand = candidates_of(laysinit)\n    acticand = candidates_of(actiinit)\n    weigcand = candidates_of(weiginit)\n    biascand = candidates_of(biasinit)\n\n    layersize = Vote.layersize_from(layscand)\n    activfunc = Vote.activfunc_from(acticand)\n    weigvalue = Vote.weigvalue_from(weigcand)\n    biasvalue = Vote.biasvalue_from(biascand)\n\n    return Tnn(\n        layersize=layersize,\n        activfunc=activfunc,\n        weigvalue=weigvalue,\n        biasvalue=biasvalue)", "Program",
 Evaluatable->False,
 AutoIndent->False,
 LineBreakWithin->False,
 PageWidth->Infinity,
 CellTags->"code:tgpdef.py"]

}, Open]]

}, Open]]

}, Open]],

